# Styles: the properties of an element (Gap, Marker, Column sizes...) given once in a rule.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Styles · Element properties in rules
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: dish
			Gap: 12
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
				Padding: 0 0 6 0
				Border: 0 0 0.5 0
				Border color: rule
		For style: name
			Grow: 1
		For style: price
			Typography:
				Bold: true
		For element: List
			Marker: dash
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 14
		For element: Table
			Column sizes: * 70
			Column align: left right
		For element: Cell
			Box:
				Padding: 3 6
	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Element properties in rules
		Paragraph: Besides `Box`, `Typography` and `Break`, a rule gives the properties that say how an element looks or distributes its content: the `Gap` of a `Stack`, the `Marker` of a `List`, the `Column sizes` of a `Table`. `Grow`, `Shrink` and `Base size` belong to the `Item` and come from the rule of the element inside it.
			Style: intro
		Text: For style: dish (Gap: 12) and For style: name (Grow: 1)
			Style: label
		Stack:
			Style: dish
			Item:
				Text: Red prawn croquettes
					Style: name
			Item:
				Text: 9.50
					Style: price
		Stack:
			Style: dish
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
			Item:
				Text: Confit artichokes with ham
					Style: name
			Item:
				Text: 12.00
					Style: price
		Text: For element: List (Marker: dash)
			Style: label
		List:
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
			List item:
				Paragraph: The list declares no marker: the rule gives it.
			List item:
				Paragraph: Every list of the document gets the same one.
		Text: For element: Table (Column sizes: * 70, Column align: left right)
			Style: label
		Table:
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Walnut chair
					Cell: 145.00
				Row:
					Cell: Dining table
					Cell: 890.00
